cit - a strengthening of the proof, never a weakening of what the item provides); lem-nat-mult-cancellative (Facts/step-tag/deps/URL-level repair; Statement, Definition and title unchanged); lem-nat-nonzero-is-successor (Facts/step-tag/deps/URL-level repair; Statement, Definition and title unchanged); lem-nat-order-mult-compatible (Facts/step-tag/deps/URL-level repair; Statement, Definition and title unchanged); lem-nat-successor-neq-self (Facts/step-tag/deps/URL-level repair; Statement, Definition and title unchanged); lem-nat-transitive-irreflexive (Facts/step-tag/deps/URL-level repair; Statement, Definition and title unchanged); lem-rat-embeds-dense (STATEMENT-LEVEL OVERCLAIM REPAIRED BY PROOF at A8 round 3, on owner instruction. The Statement always said the map is \"an embedding of ordered fields\" and step 4.1 said \"ordered subfield\", but the proof never touched multiplicative inverses. The repair PROVES the missing half rather than narrowing the claim: deps += thm-reals-field, [L2] extended to supply reciprocals in Q, a new [L5] recording that R = C/N is a field with 0_R and 1_R the constant classes and that inverses there are unique, and a new step 2.2 deriving (q-hat)^{-1} = (1/q)-hat. The change is PURELY ADDITIVE - title, Statement and every pre-existing step (1.1, 1.2, 2.1, 3.1) are untouched, and the only deletions are the three lines rewritten in place. No consumer can therefore lose a licence; on the contrary the six consumers that actually assert the field-embedding property (ex-completion-of-q-is-r [L1], lem-cauchy-with-convergent-subsequence [L3], def-sequence, cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected [L5], thm-euler-totient-product-formula [L6], rem-sequence-conventions) were UNDER-licensed before and are fully licensed now. This is the mirror image of the lem-rat-cut-embeds narrowing, which is why no consumer repair was needed here); lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space (Statement unchanged; one Remark corrected for published-claim decay); thm-