research/audit/wave4-foundations.findings.md-90-> [L10] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha=\beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; a function is injective when equality of two values forces equality of the corresponding inputs ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-well-order]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
