research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4879-**The hierarchy, and its exhaustiveness.** The Hartogs number gives a successor
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4880-cardinal in ZF ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]); transfinite recursion along
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4881-the ordinals turns the successor clause into the alephs, and the power clause
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:4882:into the beths ([[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:4883:[[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]). That the alephs are not merely a supply of
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4884-infinite cardinals but **all** of them is a separate theorem, proved by a least
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4885-counterexample rather than by the recursion, and its second clause — that every
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4886-infinite *set* is equinumerous with an aleph — is where the Axiom of Choice
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-4887-enters ([[thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph]]).
