research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6690-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6691-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6692-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6693-**Given:** ZF; the Axiom of Choice only in clause (b).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6694-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:6695:[L1] The operation $\alpha \mapsto \aleph_\alpha$ is defined at every ordinal, takes infinite cardinal values, is strictly increasing, satisfies $\aleph_0 = \omega$, $\aleph_{\alpha+1} = \aleph_\alpha^{+}$, $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at limits, and satisfies $\alpha \le \aleph_\alpha$ ([[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6696-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6697-[L2] $\kappa^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above the cardinal $\kappa$ ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6698-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-6699-[L3] Every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; ordinals satisfy trichotomy; $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$; an ordinal is a transitive set ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-ordinal]]).
