research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7254-[L1] $\operatorname{cf}(\alpha) \le \alpha$; for a limit ordinal $\lambda$, $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal; every cofinal $C \subseteq \lambda$ has $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lvert C\rvert$ ([[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinality]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7255-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7256-[L2] $\operatorname{cf}(\alpha)$ is the least length of a cofinal map into $\alpha$, and a strictly increasing cofinal map of that length exists ([[def-cofinality]], [[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7257-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:7258:[L3] $\aleph_0 = \omega$; $\aleph_{\alpha+1} = \aleph_\alpha^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above $\aleph_\alpha$; $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at limits; every $\aleph_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal and the operation is strictly increasing ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]], [[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7259-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7260-[L4] Every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal, and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-limit-ordinal]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7261-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-7262-[L5] For an infinite cardinal $\mu$ and a cardinal $\nu$ with $0 \ne \nu \le \mu$, $\mu \otimes \nu = \mu$ ([[cor-cardinal-absorption]], [[thm-hessenberg]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
