research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8652-so $\beth_\omega$ is singular ([[def-cofinality]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8653-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8654-The first three values are the definition unwound, once
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8655-$\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert = 2^{\aleph_0}$ is known
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8656:([[ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum]]) and once
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8657-$2^{\lvert A \rvert} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(A)\rvert$ is available for an arbitrary
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8658-set ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]]). The last is the same cofinality
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8659-argument that applies to $\aleph_\omega$, and for the same reason: the index
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8660-$\omega$ is a limit reached by an $\omega$-indexed family, and the beth operation
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8661-is continuous at limits.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8662-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8663-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8664-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8665-**Given:** The Axiom of Choice.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8666-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8667:[L1] $\beth_0 = \omega$, $\beth_{\alpha+1} = 2^{\beth_\alpha}$, and $\beth_\lambda = \bigcup\{\beth_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at a limit $\lambda$; every $\beth_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal and the operation is strictly increasing; $\aleph_0 = \omega$ ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8668-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8669-[L2] $2^{\lvert A \rvert} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(A)\rvert$ for every set $A$, and $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8670-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8671:[L3] $\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert = 2^{\aleph_0}$ ([[ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8672-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8673-[L4] $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\lvert \alpha\rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-equinumerous]]); assuming the Axiom of Choice every set has a cardinality ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8674-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8675-[L5] For a limit ordinal $\lambda$: $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal, and every cofinal $C \subseteq \lambda$ satisfies $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lvert C\rvert$ ([[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinality]], [[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8676-
--
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8696-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8697-**Where the beths and the alephs are known to agree, and where they are not.** $\beth_0 = \aleph_0$ by the base clauses. Beyond that, this development proves $\aleph_1 \le \beth_1$ ([[ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum]]) and nothing sharper: whether $\beth_1 = \aleph_1$ is the continuum hypothesis, which [[rem-cardinal-arithmetic-choice-ledger]] records as undecided by the axioms in use here.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8698-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8699-**Why $\beth_2$ is written two ways.** As $2^{2^{\aleph_0}}$ it is a cardinal computation; as $\lvert \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R})\rvert$ it is a statement about a familiar set. The bridge is the general clause $2^{\lvert A\rvert} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(A)\rvert$ of [[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]], applied at $A = \mathbb{R}$; without it the two expressions would have to be related by hand.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8700-
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8701:**Singularity at a limit index is generic, not special to $\beth_\omega$.** The computation of step 2.2 uses only that the operation is strictly increasing and continuous at $\omega$, so it applies verbatim to $\aleph_\omega$ ([[ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega]]) and to the fixed-point tower of [[ex-an-aleph-fixed-point]]. What is not generic is the value of the cofinality at other limit indices, which depends on the index and not on the operation.
