research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8951:cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined facts=9 steps=8
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8952-L1 => lem-recursion-on-the-ordinals :: A class rule $G$ assigning a set to every function whose domain is an ordinal determines exactly one class function $F$, defined at every ordinal, with $F(\beta) = G(F \restriction \beta)$ ([[lem-recursion-on-the-ordinals]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8953-L2 => lem-successor-cardinal-exists :: $\aleph(A)$ is a cardinal for every set $A$; for a cardinal $\kappa$ it is the least cardinal strictly above $\kappa$; and it is infinite when $\kappa$ is ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8954-L3 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal,def-limit-ordinal :: $\omega$ is a cardinal, and every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[def-limit-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8955-L4 => lem-ordinal-basics,lem-ordinal-trichotomy :: For a set $A$ of ordinals, $\bigcup A$ is an ordinal and is the least upper bound of $A$; ordinals satisfy trichotomy; $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8956-L5 => def-limit-ordinal :: Every ordinal is exactly one of $0$, a successor, or a limit ([[def-limit-ordinal]]).
--
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8965-3.1 :: Strict increase for the alephs: $\aleph_\gamma \in \aleph_{\gamma+1}$ by [L2] and step 2.1; at a limit $\lambda$ with $\gamma \in \lambda$ we have $\gamma + 1 \in \lambda$ by [L4] and [L5], so $\aleph_\gamma \in \aleph_{\gamma+1} \subseteq \aleph_\lambda$; and the general case $\alpha \in \beta \Rightarrow \aleph_\alpha \in \aleph_\beta$ follows by transfinite induction on $\beta$ along [L9]. [step 2.1, L2, L4, L5, L9]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8966-3.2 :: Strict increase for the beths is the same argument with [L8] in place of [L2]. [step 2.2, L4, L5, L8, L9]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8967-4.1 :: Claim (c), by transfinite induction on $\alpha$ along [L9]: $0 \le \aleph_0$; if $\gamma \le \aleph_\gamma$ then $\aleph_{\gamma+1} > \aleph_\gamma \ge \gamma$ by step 3.1, so $\aleph_{\gamma+1} \ge \gamma + 1$ by [L4]; and at a limit $\lambda$, every $\gamma \in \lambda$ satisfies $\gamma \le \aleph_\gamma \in \aleph_{\gamma+1} \subseteq \aleph_\lambda$ by step 3.1 and [L4], so $\gamma \in \aleph_\lambda$ and hence $\lambda \subseteq \aleph_\lambda$. [step 3.1, L4, L9]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8968-5.1 :: So both operations exist, are unique, take infinite cardinal values, are strictly increasing, and are continuous at limits by the third clause of step 1.1 read through [L4]; and $\alpha \le \aleph_\alpha$ throughout. [step 2.1, step 2.2, step 3.1, step 3.2, step 4.1] ∎
