research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:8973:L1 => cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined,def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies :: The operation $\alpha \mapsto \aleph_\alpha$ is defined at every ordinal, takes infinite cardinal values, is strictly increasing, satisfies $\aleph_0 = \omega$, $\aleph_{\alpha+1} = \aleph_\alpha^{+}$, $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at limits, and satisfies $\alpha \le \aleph_\alpha$ ([[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8974-L2 => lem-successor-cardinal-exists :: $\kappa^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above the cardinal $\kappa$ ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8975-L3 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy,lem-ordinal-basics,def-ordinal :: Every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; ordinals satisfy trichotomy; $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$; an ordinal is a transitive set ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8976-L4 => def-limit-ordinal,lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal :: Every ordinal is exactly one of $0$, a successor, or a limit ([[def-limit-ordinal]]); $\omega$ is the least limit ordinal ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8977-L5 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-cardinal :: A cardinal $\kappa$ is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$, and $\omega$ is a cardinal ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-8978-L6 => lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set :: For a well-orderable $X$, $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, $X \approx \lvert X \rvert$, it is a cardinal, and $\lvert \alpha \rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]]).
