research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9046-L1 => thm-cofinality-basics,def-cofinality :: $\operatorname{cf}(\alpha) \le \alpha$; for a limit ordinal $\lambda$, $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal; every cofinal $C \subseteq \lambda$ has $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lvert C\rvert$ ([[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinality]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9047-L2 => def-cofinality,lem-cofinality-is-well-defined :: $\operatorname{cf}(\alpha)$ is the least length of a cofinal map into $\alpha$, and a strictly increasing cofinal map of that length exists ([[def-cofinality]], [[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9048:L3 => def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined,lem-successor-cardinal-exists :: $\aleph_0 = \omega$; $\aleph_{\alpha+1} = \aleph_\alpha^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above $\aleph_\alpha$; $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at limits; every $\aleph_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal and the operation is strictly increasing ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]], [[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9049-L4 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-limit-ordinal,def-cardinal :: Every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal, and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-limit-ordinal]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9050-L5 => cor-cardinal-absorption,thm-hessenberg,def-cardinal-arithmetic :: For an infinite cardinal $\mu$ and a cardinal $\nu$ with $0 \ne \nu \le \mu$, $\mu \otimes \nu = \mu$ ([[cor-cardinal-absorption]], [[thm-hessenberg]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9051-L6 => lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws :: For cardinals $\kappa \le \lambda$ iff $\kappa \preceq \lambda$; $A \preceq B$ with both well-orderable gives $\lvert A\rvert \le \lvert B\rvert$; $\otimes$ is monotone ([[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9052-L7 => lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set,def-equinumerous :: $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, satisfies $X \approx \lvert X\rvert$ and $\lvert \alpha\rvert \le \alpha$, and equals $\alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-equinumerous]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9053-L8 => def-axiom-of-choice,def-choice-function :: Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function ([[def-axiom-of-choice]], [[def-choice-function]]).
