research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9100-L1 => cor-cardinal-absorption :: For an infinite cardinal $\nu$ and a cardinal $\rho \le \nu$: $\nu \oplus \rho = \nu$ ([[cor-cardinal-absorption]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9101-L2 => lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws :: $\oplus$ is commutative ([[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9102-L3 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-cardinal-arithmetic :: Every natural number is a cardinal, $\omega$ is a cardinal, and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9103:L4 => def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal :: $\aleph_0 = \omega$ ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]); $\omega$ is the least limit ordinal and $1 \in \omega$ ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9104-L5 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy,lem-ordinal-basics :: Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, and $\alpha \notin \alpha$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9105-1.1 :: Suppose, for contradiction, that the displayed claim holds for all cardinals $\kappa, \lambda, \mu$. [assume-contra]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9106-1.2 :: By [L3] and [L4] the ordinals $1$ and $\aleph_0 = \omega$ are cardinals, $\aleph_0$ is infinite, $1 \in \aleph_0$ and hence $1 \le \aleph_0$, and $1 \ne \aleph_0$ by [L5]. [L3, L4, L5]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9107-2.1 :: By [L1] with $\nu = \aleph_0$ and $\rho = \aleph_0$, $\aleph_0 \oplus \aleph_0 = \aleph_0$; and by [L2] and [L1] with $\rho = 1$, $1 \oplus \aleph_0 = \aleph_0 \oplus 1 = \aleph_0$. [step 1.2, L1, L2]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9108-3.1 :: So the hypothesis of the assumed claim holds at $\kappa = \aleph_0$, $\lambda = 1$, $\mu = \aleph_0$, and the claim would give $\aleph_0 = 1$, which step 1.2 forbids; therefore cardinal addition is not cancellative. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 2.1, discharge-contradiction] ∎
