research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9110-fs-every-aleph-is-regular facts=4 steps=3
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9111-L1 => thm-regularity-of-the-alephs :: $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) = \aleph_0$, and $\aleph_0 < \aleph_\omega$, so $\aleph_\omega$ is singular; this is a theorem of ZF (clause (c) of [[thm-regularity-of-the-alephs]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9112-L2 => def-cofinality,def-cardinal :: A cardinal $\kappa$ is regular when $\operatorname{cf}(\kappa) = \kappa$ ([[def-cofinality]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9113:L3 => cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined :: The operation $\alpha \mapsto \aleph_\alpha$ is defined at every ordinal and is strictly increasing ([[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9114-L4 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy,lem-ordinal-basics :: Ordinals satisfy trichotomy and $\alpha \notin \alpha$, so $\alpha < \beta$ and $\alpha = \beta$ cannot both hold ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9115-1.1 :: Suppose, for contradiction, that $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\alpha) = \aleph_\alpha$ for every ordinal $\alpha$. [assume-contra]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9116-1.2 :: By [L1] and [L3], $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) = \aleph_0$ and $\aleph_0 < \aleph_\omega$. [L1, L3]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9117-2.1 :: Instantiating the assumption at $\alpha = \omega$ gives $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) = \aleph_\omega$, hence $\aleph_0 = \aleph_\omega$ by step 1.2, which [L4] forbids; so not every aleph is regular, and $\aleph_\omega$ is singular by [L2]. [step 1.1, step 1.2, L2, L4, discharge-contradiction] ∎
