research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9120-L1 => lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws :: $\kappa \le \lambda$ implies $\kappa^{\mu} \le \lambda^{\mu}$; and $(\mu^{\nu})^{\rho} = \mu^{\nu \otimes \rho}$ ([[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9121-L2 => thm-hessenberg :: $\kappa \otimes \kappa = \kappa$ for every infinite cardinal $\kappa$ ([[thm-hessenberg]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9122-L3 => thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor :: $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ and $2^{\kappa}$ is a cardinal ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9123:L4 => def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,lem-successor-cardinal-exists,cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined :: $\aleph_1 = \aleph_0^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above $\aleph_0$, and $\aleph_0 < \aleph_1$ ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9124:L5 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-cardinal,def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies :: $\aleph_0 = \omega$ is an infinite cardinal and $2 \in \omega$ is a cardinal with $2 \le \aleph_0$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9125-L6 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy,lem-ordinal-basics :: Ordinals satisfy trichotomy and $\alpha \notin \alpha$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9126-1.1 :: Suppose, for contradiction, that $\kappa < \lambda$ implies $\kappa^{\mu} < \lambda^{\mu}$ for all cardinals. [assume-contra]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9127-1.2 :: By [L3] the cardinal $2^{\aleph_0}$ satisfies $\aleph_0 < 2^{\aleph_0}$, so [L4] gives $\aleph_1 \le 2^{\aleph_0}$; with [L5] this chains to $2 \le \aleph_0 < \aleph_1 \le 2^{\aleph_0}$. [L3, L4, L5]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9128-2.1 :: Applying [L1] along that chain, $2^{\aleph_0} \le \aleph_0^{\aleph_0} \le \aleph_1^{\aleph_0} \le (2^{\aleph_0})^{\aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_0 \otimes \aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_0}$, the last two equalities by [L1] and [L2]; so all four values are equal and in particular $\aleph_0^{\aleph_0} = \aleph_1^{\aleph_0}$. [step 1.2, L1, L2, L5, L6]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9129-3.1 :: But $\aleph_0 < \aleph_1$ by step 1.2, so the assumed claim at $\kappa = \aleph_0$, $\lambda = \aleph_1$, $\mu = \aleph_0$ gives $\aleph_0^{\aleph_0} < \aleph_1^{\aleph_0}$, contradicting step 2.1 by [L6]; therefore exponentiation is not strictly monotone in the base. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 2.1, L6, discharge-contradiction] ∎
