research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9136-1.1 :: Suppose, for contradiction, that $2^{\aleph_0} = \aleph_\omega$. [assume-contra]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9137-1.2 :: By [L1] and [L3], $\operatorname{cf}(2^{\aleph_0}) > \aleph_0$. [L1, L3]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9138-1.3 :: By [L2], $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) = \aleph_0$. [L2]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9139-2.1 :: Equal ordinals have equal cofinalities, so the assumption turns step 1.3 into $\operatorname{cf}(2^{\aleph_0}) = \aleph_0$, contradicting step 1.2 by [L4]; therefore $2^{\aleph_0} \ne \aleph_\omega$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 1.3, L4, discharge-contradiction] ∎
