research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9176-L1 => thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor,def-cardinal-arithmetic,def-cardinal :: $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ and $2^{\kappa}$ is a cardinal, for every cardinal $\kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9177:L2 => lem-successor-cardinal-exists,def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,def-first-uncountable-ordinal,thm-omega-one-is-the-least-uncountable-ordinal :: $\aleph_1 = \aleph_0^{+}$ is the least cardinal strictly above $\aleph_0$, and $\aleph_0 < \aleph_1$; also $\aleph_1 = \omega_1$ ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[def-first-uncountable-ordinal]], [[thm-omega-one-is-the-least-uncountable-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9178-L3 => thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph :: Every infinite cardinal is $\aleph_\alpha$ for exactly one ordinal $\alpha$, and the enumeration is strictly increasing ([[thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9179:L4 => ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum,lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set :: $\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert = 2^{\aleph_0}$ and $\mathbb{R} \approx \lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert$ ([[ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum]], [[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9180-L5 => lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws,def-equinumerous,def-injection-surjection-bijection :: For cardinals $\kappa \le \lambda$ iff $\kappa \preceq \lambda$ (claim (a) of [[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]], [[def-equinumerous]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9181-L6 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy :: Ordinals satisfy trichotomy ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9182-1.1 :: By [L1] at $\kappa = \aleph_0$, the value $2^{\aleph_0}$ is a cardinal with $\aleph_0 < 2^{\aleph_0}$. [L1]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9183-1.2 :: By [L2], $\aleph_1$ is the least cardinal strictly above $\aleph_0$, and $\aleph_1 = \omega_1$. [L2]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9184-2.1 :: Steps 1.1 and 1.2 give $\aleph_1 \le 2^{\aleph_0}$ directly from minimality; hence $\omega_1 = \aleph_1 \preceq 2^{\aleph_0} = \lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert \approx \mathbb{R}$ by [L5] and [L4], so $\omega_1$ injects into $\mathbb{R}$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, L4, L5]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9185-3.1 :: Finally $2^{\aleph_0}$ is an infinite cardinal by step 1.1, so $2^{\aleph_0} = \aleph_\alpha$ for exactly one $\alpha$ by [L3], and $\alpha = 0$ is excluded because $\aleph_0 < 2^{\aleph_0}$, so $1 \le \alpha$ by [L6]. [step 1.1, step 2.1, L3, L6] ∎
