research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9187:ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega facts=6 steps=5
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9188:L1 => def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined :: $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at a limit ordinal $\lambda$; every $\aleph_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal; the operation is strictly increasing ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9189-L2 => lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal,def-limit-ordinal,thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-cardinal :: $\omega$ is a limit ordinal ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[def-limit-ordinal]]); every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9190-L3 => def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal :: $C \subseteq \alpha$ is cofinal when every $\zeta \in \alpha$ has some $\eta \in C$ with $\zeta \le \eta$ ([[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9191-L4 => thm-cofinality-basics,def-cofinality :: For a limit ordinal $\lambda$: $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal, and every cofinal $C \subseteq \lambda$ satisfies $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lvert C\rvert$ ([[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinality]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9192-L5 => lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set,def-equinumerous :: $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, and equinumerous sets receive the same one ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-equinumerous]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9193-L6 => lem-ordinal-trichotomy,lem-ordinal-basics,def-injection-surjection-bijection :: Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, and $\alpha \subseteq \beta \subseteq \alpha$ forces $\alpha = \beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
--
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9195-1.2 :: $C$ is cofinal in $\aleph_\omega$: by [L1] and [L2], $\aleph_\omega = \bigcup C$, so each $\zeta \in \aleph_\omega$ lies in some $\aleph_n$ and hence satisfies $\zeta \le \aleph_n$ with $\aleph_n \in C$, which is [L3]. [L1, L2, L3, L6]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9196-1.3 :: $\lvert C\rvert = \aleph_0$: the map $n \mapsto \aleph_n$ is injective by the strict increase in [L1], so $C \approx \omega$ and [L5] applies. [L1, L5]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9197-2.1 :: By [L4] with $\lambda = \aleph_\omega$, which is a limit ordinal by [L1] and [L2], steps 1.2 and 1.3 give $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) \le \aleph_0$; and $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega)$ is an infinite cardinal by [L4], so $\aleph_0 \le \operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega)$ by [L2]. [step 1.2, step 1.3, L1, L2, L4]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9198-3.1 :: Hence $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_\omega) = \aleph_0$ by [L6], and $\aleph_0 < \aleph_\omega$ by the strict increase in [L1], so $\aleph_\omega$ is singular. [step 2.1, L1, L6] ∎
