research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9231:ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed facts=7 steps=5
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9232:L1 => def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies,cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined :: $\beth_0 = \omega$, $\beth_{\alpha+1} = 2^{\beth_\alpha}$, and $\beth_\lambda = \bigcup\{\beth_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ at a limit $\lambda$; every $\beth_\alpha$ is an infinite cardinal and the operation is strictly increasing; $\aleph_0 = \omega$ ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]], [[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9233-L2 => thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor,def-cardinal-arithmetic :: $2^{\lvert A \rvert} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(A)\rvert$ for every set $A$, and $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:9234:L3 => ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum :: $\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert = 2^{\aleph_0}$ ([[ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9235-L4 => lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set,def-cardinal,def-equinumerous,thm-well-ordering-theorem :: $\lvert X\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\lvert \alpha\rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-equinumerous]]); assuming the Axiom of Choice every set has a cardinality ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9236-L5 => thm-cofinality-basics,def-cofinality,def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal :: For a limit ordinal $\lambda$: $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal, and every cofinal $C \subseteq \lambda$ satisfies $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lvert C\rvert$ ([[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinality]], [[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9237-L6 => thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting,def-limit-ordinal :: Every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal, and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-limit-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9238-L7 => lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal,lem-ordinal-basics,lem-ordinal-trichotomy,def-injection-surjection-bijection :: $\omega$ is a limit ordinal ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]]); ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\bigcup$ of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9239-1.1 :: $\beth_0 = \omega = \aleph_0$, by the two base clauses in [L1]. [L1]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9240-1.2 :: The set $C = \{\beth_n : n \in \omega\}$ exists by Replacement, is contained in $\beth_\omega$ by the strict increase in [L1], and is cofinal in $\beth_\omega = \bigcup C$, since every $\zeta \in \beth_\omega$ lies in some $\beth_n$ and hence satisfies $\zeta \le \beth_n$; and $n \mapsto \beth_n$ is injective by that same strict increase, so $C \approx \omega$ and $\lvert C\rvert = \aleph_0$ by [L4] and [L1]. [L1, L4, L7]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9241-2.1 :: $\beth_1 = 2^{\beth_0} = 2^{\aleph_0}$ by [L1] and step 1.1, and this equals $\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert$ by [L3]. [step 1.1, L1, L3]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9242-2.2 :: $\beth_\omega$ is an infinite cardinal by [L1], hence a limit ordinal by [L6], so [L5] applied to step 1.2 gives $\operatorname{cf}(\beth_\omega) \le \aleph_0$, while $\operatorname{cf}(\beth_\omega)$ is an infinite cardinal by [L5] and so $\aleph_0 \le \operatorname{cf}(\beth_\omega)$ by [L6]; hence $\operatorname{cf}(\beth_\omega) = \aleph_0$ by [L7], and $\aleph_0 = \beth_0 < \beth_\omega$ by the strict increase in [L1]. [step 1.2, L1, L5, L6, L7]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-9243-3.1 :: $\beth_2 = 2^{\beth_1} = 2^{\lvert \mathbb{R}\rvert} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R})\rvert$ by [L1], step 2.1 and [L2]; and $2^{\beth_1} = 2^{2^{\aleph_0}}$ by step 2.1. [step 2.1, L1, L2] ∎
