research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-11661-5:1.1 Claim (a): $\omega$ is a limit ordinal by [L9], so $\operatorname{cf}(\omega)$ is an infinite cardinal by [L1], hence $\omega \le \operatorname{cf}(\omega)$ by [L4]; and $\operatorname{cf}(\omega) \le \omega$ by [L1], so $\operatorname{cf}(\aleph_0) = \aleph_0$. [L1, L3, L4, L9]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-11662-7:1.2 The set $C = \{\aleph_n : n \in \omega\}$ exists by Replacement, is contained in $\aleph_\omega$ and is cofinal in it, since $\aleph_\omega = \bigcup C$ by [L3] means every $\zeta \in \aleph_\omega$ lies in some $\aleph_n$ and hence satisfies $\zeta \le \aleph_n$; moreover $n \mapsto \aleph_n$ is injective by the strict increase in [L3], so $C \approx \omega$ and $\lvert C\rvert = \aleph_0$ by [L7]. [L3, L7, L9]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-11663-9:1.3 Setting up claim (b): let $\lambda = \aleph_\alpha$, $\kappa = \aleph_{\alpha+1}$, and suppose $\beta = \operatorname{cf}(\kappa) < \kappa$, with $g : \beta \to \kappa$ strictly increasing and cofinal by [L2]; then $\kappa$ is a limit ordinal by [L4], so $\beta$ is an infinite cardinal by [L1], and $\beta \le \lambda$ because $\beta$ is a cardinal below the least cardinal strictly above $\lambda$ ([L3]); moreover $\kappa = \bigcup\{g(\xi) : \xi \in \beta\}$, since for $\zeta \in \kappa$ the ordinal $\zeta \cup \{\zeta\}$ also lies in $\kappa$ and is $\le g(\xi)$ for some $\xi$, putting $\zeta \in g(\xi)$. [L1, L2, L3, L4, L9]
