research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-11684-5:1.1 By [L6] and [L3], $2 \le \aleph_0 \le 2^{\aleph_0}$; so [L1] gives $2^{\aleph_0} \le \aleph_0^{\aleph_0} \le (2^{\aleph_0})^{\aleph_0}$, and $(2^{\aleph_0})^{\aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_0 \otimes \aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_0}$ by [L1] and [L2]; therefore $\aleph_0^{\aleph_0} = 2^{\aleph_0}$ by [L7]. [L1, L2, L3, L6, L7]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-11685-9:2.1 $\mathfrak{c}^{\mathfrak{c}} = (2^{\aleph_0})^{\mathfrak{c}} = 2^{\aleph_0 \otimes \mathfrak{c}} = 2^{\mathfrak{c}}$: the middle equality is the second exponent law in [L1], and the last is absorption in [L2], applicable because $\mathfrak{c}$ is an infinite cardinal with $0 \ne \aleph_0 \le \mathfrak{c}$ by [L3] and [L6]. [step 1.2, L1, L2, L3, L6]
