research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596341-+ ['thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[C,H],'The sources state that finite cardinal arithmetic agrees with finite counting. The item adds the exact identification with the library natural operations, finite-cardinality definition, and the separate ordinal addition/product agreement.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596342-+ ['thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources identify 2^kappa with the power-set cardinal and state Cantor strictness. The item recasts the ZF combinatorial theorem under the library convention that the displayed cardinal exponent and arbitrary cardinalities are named under AC.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596343-+ ['thm-hessenberg','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[K],'The source states the same theorem for every infinite cardinal, kappa times kappa equals kappa, and gives the standard well-order-of-pairs proof. The item expands that proof and makes its absence of choice explicit.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596344-+ ['cor-cardinal-absorption','literature-derived','ai-generated','exact-source',[C],'The source states the same sum and product absorption laws for an infinite cardinal and a smaller cardinal, including the nonzero condition for multiplication. The item derives the result locally from Hessenberg and comparison.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596345-+ ['lem-successor-cardinal-exists','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources construct the Hartogs number and the successor cardinal. The item packages cardinality, strictness, minimality, and infinitude in one ZF lemma and supplies its own detailed injection argument.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596346:+ ['cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,C],'The standard aleph and beth recursions, strict increase, and limit continuity are sourced. The item turns their formula-level existence and uniqueness into a separate corollary and splits the ZF aleph clauses from its AC-based beth convention.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596347:+ ['def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[K,C],'The sources give the successor, limit, aleph, and beth clauses. The item adds the local successor-cardinal notation rule, the ZF/AC split, and the identifications aleph_0=omega and aleph_1=omega_1.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596348-+ ['thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources enumerate the infinite cardinals by the alephs. The item separates the ZF assertion about cardinal ordinals from the AC assertion about arbitrary infinite sets and proves uniqueness locally.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596349-+ ['thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[E,K],'The sources state exactly that comparability by injection for every pair of sets is equivalent over ZF to the Axiom of Choice. The proof is the standard well-ordering/Hartogs argument, expanded into the library dependency language.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596350-+ ['thm-tarski-square','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[T],'The source states Tarski\'s exact equivalence over ZF: AC iff every infinite set is equinumerous with its square. The item supplies an adapted cardinal/Hartogs proof with finite stages made explicit.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596351-+ ['lem-cofinality-is-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sources characterize cofinality by a shortest cofinal map and show that a monotone or strictly increasing witness may be used. The item extends the convention to every ordinal and constructs the strict witness by a local recursion.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596352-+ ['def-cofinality','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition.'],
