research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596361-+ ['fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated strengthening of weak base monotonicity. Its truth risk is discharged by the displayed ZFC witness aleph_0<aleph_1 but aleph_0^aleph_0=aleph_1^aleph_0=2^aleph_0.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596362-+ ['fs-the-continuum-has-cardinality-aleph-omega','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a bespoke candidate value chosen for refutation, not a sourced assertion. Its truth risk is discharged because cf(2^aleph_0)>aleph_0 whereas cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596363:+ ['ex-cardinal-absorption-computed','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact four-computation bundle is a bespoke example, and every equality follows directly from cardinal absorption plus the displayed finite/countable identifications. The verification checks the nonzero and order hypotheses for each instance.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596364:+ ['ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[H],'The source states |R|=2^aleph_0. The item strengthens the presentation by separating a choice-free chain R approximately 2^omega approximately P(N) from its AC cardinal notation and by choosing Cantor-set and rational-cut injections.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-596365-+ ['ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'This exact example is a direct two-step consequence of Cantor strictness and the minimality of the successor cardinal: aleph_0<2^aleph_0 forces aleph_1<=2^aleph_0. The aleph-index and injection conclusions are then immediate from the cited definitions.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596366:+ ['ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[M],'The source explicitly gives cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha) at limit indices, hence cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0, with the same cofinal aleph sequence. The item expands the ZF upper- and lower-bound verification.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596367:+ ['ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M],'The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha), whose alpha=omega_1 instance is the displayed result. The item weakens the ambient hypothesis to AC_omega and writes out the bounded-countable-subset argument, so the hypothesis convention is not exact.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596368:+ ['ex-an-aleph-fixed-point','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[O,M],'The sources construct aleph fixed points by omega iteration of the continuous aleph operation, including singular fixed points of countable cofinality. The item selects the tower starting at aleph_0 and expands both the fixed-point and cofinality checks.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596369:+ ['ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact bundle is a bespoke unwinding of the beth definition: the first three values follow by substitution and power-set cardinality, and the beth_omega cofinality computation repeats the cited limit-sequence argument.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:596370:+ ['ex-counting-functions-and-subsets-of-the-continuum','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact pair of computations is a bespoke squeeze. Weak monotonicity, absorption, the exponent laws, and |R|=2^aleph_0 directly give aleph_0^aleph_0=2^aleph_0 and |R^R|=2^(2^aleph_0).'],
