research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604509:+ ['cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,C],'The standard aleph and beth recursions, strict increase, and limit continuity are sourced. The item turns their formula-level existence and uniqueness into a separate corollary and splits the ZF aleph clauses from its AC-based beth convention.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604510:+ ['def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[K,C],'The sources give the successor, limit, aleph, and beth clauses. The item adds the local successor-cardinal notation rule, the ZF/AC split, and the identifications aleph_0=omega and aleph_1=omega_1.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604511-+ ['thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources enumerate the infinite cardinals by the alephs. The item separates the ZF assertion about cardinal ordinals from the AC assertion about arbitrary infinite sets and proves uniqueness locally.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604512-+ ['thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[E,K],'The sources state exactly that comparability by injection for every pair of sets is equivalent over ZF to the Axiom of Choice. The proof is the standard well-ordering/Hartogs argument, expanded into the library dependency language.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604513-+ ['thm-tarski-square','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[T],'The source states Tarski\'s exact equivalence over ZF: AC iff every infinite set is equinumerous with its square. The item supplies an adapted cardinal/Hartogs proof with finite stages made explicit.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604514-+ ['lem-cofinality-is-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sources characterize cofinality by a shortest cofinal map and show that a monotone or strictly increasing witness may be used. The item extends the convention to every ordinal and constructs the strict witness by a local recursion.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604515-+ ['def-cofinality','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition.'],
