research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604526:+ ['ex-cardinal-absorption-computed','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact four-computation bundle is a bespoke example, and every equality follows directly from cardinal absorption plus the displayed finite/countable identifications. The verification checks the nonzero and order hypotheses for each instance.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604527:+ ['ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[H],'The source states |R|=2^aleph_0. The item strengthens the presentation by separating a choice-free chain R approximately 2^omega approximately P(N) from its AC cardinal notation and by choosing Cantor-set and rational-cut injections.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-604528-+ ['ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'This exact example is a direct two-step consequence of Cantor strictness and the minimality of the successor cardinal: aleph_0<2^aleph_0 forces aleph_1<=2^aleph_0. The aleph-index and injection conclusions are then immediate from the cited definitions.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604529:+ ['ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[M],'The source explicitly gives cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha) at limit indices, hence cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0, with the same cofinal aleph sequence. The item expands the ZF upper- and lower-bound verification.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:604530:+ ['ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M],'The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha), whose alpha=omega_1 instance is the displayed result. The item weakens the ambient hypothesis to AC_omega and writes out the bounded-countable-subset argument, so the hypothesis convention is not exact.'],
