research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612262-+{"id":"thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf","https://pages.jh.edu/rrynasi1/FoundationsOFMath/Literature/Set/Hrbacek%2BJech1999IntroductionToSetTheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state that finite cardinal arithmetic agrees with finite counting. The item adds the exact identification with the library natural operations, finite-cardinality definition, and the separate ordinal addition/product agreement. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
