research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612266-+{"id":"lem-successor-cardinal-exists","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://pages.jh.edu/rrynasi1/FoundationsOFMath/Literature/Set/Hrbacek%2BJech1999IntroductionToSetTheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources construct the Hartogs number and the successor cardinal. The item packages cardinality, strictness, minimality, and infinitude in one ZF lemma and supplies its own detailed injection argument. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612267:+{"id":"cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf"],"rationale":"The standard aleph and beth recursions, strict increase, and limit continuity are sourced. The item turns their formula-level existence and uniqueness into a separate corollary and splits the ZF aleph clauses from its AC-based beth convention. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
