research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612281-+{"id":"fs-every-aleph-is-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state regularity of successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega with countable cofinality. The item reframes that standard boundary as the false universal claim that every aleph is regular. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612282-+{"id":"fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the exponent-collapse law 2<=kappa<=lambda with lambda infinite implies kappa^lambda=2^lambda, which yields the displayed aleph_0/aleph_1 witness. The item reframes it as failure of a false strict base-monotonicity claim. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612283-+{"id":"fs-the-continuum-has-cardinality-aleph-omega","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://diposit.ub.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/706acdf4-5d85-4cf5-b3fc-36d610a73954/content"],"rationale":"The sources give cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0 and the König consequence cf(2^aleph_0)>aleph_0, explicitly excluding every continuum value of countable cofinality. The item reframes that restriction as the false candidate equality 2^aleph_0=aleph_omega. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
