research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612286-+{"id":"ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"This exact example is a direct two-step consequence of Cantor strictness and the minimality of the successor cardinal: aleph_0<2^aleph_0 forces aleph_1<=2^aleph_0. The aleph-index and injection conclusions are then immediate from the cited definitions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612287:+{"id":"ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha). The item specializes it to alpha=omega, names the exact cofinal set C={aleph_n:n in omega}, and expands the choice-free upper- and lower-bound verification. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612288:+{"id":"ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha), whose alpha=omega_1 instance is the displayed result. The item weakens the ambient hypothesis to AC_omega and writes out the bounded-countable-subset argument, so the hypothesis convention is not exact. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612289:+{"id":"ex-an-aleph-fixed-point","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.osu.edu/~derdzinski.1/courses/5001/fixed-points.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources construct aleph fixed points by omega iteration of the continuous aleph operation, including singular fixed points of countable cofinality. The item selects the tower starting at aleph_0 and expands both the fixed-point and cofinality checks. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
