research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612592-+ ['thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[C,H],'The sources state that finite cardinal arithmetic agrees with finite counting. The item adds the exact identification with the library natural operations, finite-cardinality definition, and the separate ordinal addition/product agreement.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612593-+ ['thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources identify 2^kappa with the power-set cardinal and state Cantor strictness. The item recasts the ZF combinatorial theorem under the library convention that the displayed cardinal exponent and arbitrary cardinalities are named under AC.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612594-+ ['thm-hessenberg','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[K],'The source states the same theorem for every infinite cardinal, kappa times kappa equals kappa, and gives the standard well-order-of-pairs proof. The item expands that proof and makes its absence of choice explicit.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612595-+ ['cor-cardinal-absorption','literature-derived','ai-generated','exact-source',[C],'The source states the same sum and product absorption laws for an infinite cardinal and a smaller cardinal, including the nonzero condition for multiplication. The item derives the result locally from Hessenberg and comparison.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612596-+ ['lem-successor-cardinal-exists','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources construct the Hartogs number and the successor cardinal. The item packages cardinality, strictness, minimality, and infinitude in one ZF lemma and supplies its own detailed injection argument.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612597:+ ['cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,C],'The standard aleph and beth recursions, strict increase, and limit continuity are sourced. The item turns their formula-level existence and uniqueness into a separate corollary and splits the ZF aleph clauses from its AC-based beth convention.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612598:+ ['def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[K,C],'The sources give the successor, limit, aleph, and beth clauses. The item adds the local successor-cardinal notation rule, the ZF/AC split, and the identifications aleph_0=omega and aleph_1=omega_1.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612599-+ ['thm-every-infinite-cardinal-is-an-aleph','ai-altered','ai-generated','semantic-source',[K,H],'The sources enumerate the infinite cardinals by the alephs. The item separates the ZF assertion about cardinal ordinals from the AC assertion about arbitrary infinite sets and proves uniqueness locally.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612600-+ ['thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[E,K],'The sources state exactly that comparability by injection for every pair of sets is equivalent over ZF to the Axiom of Choice. The proof is the standard well-ordering/Hartogs argument, expanded into the library dependency language.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612601-+ ['thm-tarski-square','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[T],'The source states Tarski\'s exact equivalence over ZF: AC iff every infinite set is equinumerous with its square. The item supplies an adapted cardinal/Hartogs proof with finite stages made explicit.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612602-+ ['lem-cofinality-is-well-defined','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sources characterize cofinality by a shortest cofinal map and show that a monotone or strictly increasing witness may be used. The item extends the convention to every ordinal and constructs the strict witness by a local recursion.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612603-+ ['def-cofinality','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition.'],
--
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612609-+ ['rem-cardinal-arithmetic-choice-ledger','ai-generated','not-applicable','none',[],'This is positively a bespoke page-local synthesis: it inventories exactly which published items on this page use ZF, AC, or AC_omega and summarizes the local continuum boundary. Its claims were checked against every named item and proof; no independent literature counterpart to this page-specific ledger is asserted.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612610-+ ['fs-cardinal-addition-is-cancellative','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated universal overgeneralization from finite addition, selected for this library rather than recovered from a literature statement. Its falsity is verified by the explicit witness aleph_0 plus aleph_0 = 1 plus aleph_0 with aleph_0 not equal to 1.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612611-+ ['fs-every-aleph-is-regular','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated universal overgeneralization from omega and successor alephs. Its truth risk is discharged by the standard explicit counterexample cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0<aleph_omega.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612612-+ ['fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated strengthening of weak base monotonicity. Its truth risk is discharged by the displayed ZFC witness aleph_0<aleph_1 but aleph_0^aleph_0=aleph_1^aleph_0=2^aleph_0.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612613-+ ['fs-the-continuum-has-cardinality-aleph-omega','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a bespoke candidate value chosen for refutation, not a sourced assertion. Its truth risk is discharged because cf(2^aleph_0)>aleph_0 whereas cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612614:+ ['ex-cardinal-absorption-computed','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact four-computation bundle is a bespoke example, and every equality follows directly from cardinal absorption plus the displayed finite/countable identifications. The verification checks the nonzero and order hypotheses for each instance.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612615:+ ['ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[H],'The source states |R|=2^aleph_0. The item strengthens the presentation by separating a choice-free chain R approximately 2^omega approximately P(N) from its AC cardinal notation and by choosing Cantor-set and rational-cut injections.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-612616-+ ['ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'This exact example is a direct two-step consequence of Cantor strictness and the minimality of the successor cardinal: aleph_0<2^aleph_0 forces aleph_1<=2^aleph_0. The aleph-index and injection conclusions are then immediate from the cited definitions.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612617:+ ['ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega','literature-derived','ai-altered','exact-source',[M],'The source explicitly gives cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha) at limit indices, hence cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0, with the same cofinal aleph sequence. The item expands the ZF upper- and lower-bound verification.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612618:+ ['ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M],'The source gives the general limit-index identity cf(aleph_alpha)=cf(alpha), whose alpha=omega_1 instance is the displayed result. The item weakens the ambient hypothesis to AC_omega and writes out the bounded-countable-subset argument, so the hypothesis convention is not exact.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612619:+ ['ex-an-aleph-fixed-point','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[O,M],'The sources construct aleph fixed points by omega iteration of the continuous aleph operation, including singular fixed points of countable cofinality. The item selects the tower starting at aleph_0 and expands both the fixed-point and cofinality checks.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612620:+ ['ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact bundle is a bespoke unwinding of the beth definition: the first three values follow by substitution and power-set cardinality, and the beth_omega cofinality computation repeats the cited limit-sequence argument.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:612621:+ ['ex-counting-functions-and-subsets-of-the-continuum','ai-generated','ai-generated','trivial',[],'The exact pair of computations is a bespoke squeeze. Weak monotonicity, absorption, the exponent laws, and |R|=2^aleph_0 directly give aleph_0^aleph_0=2^aleph_0 and |R^R|=2^(2^aleph_0).'],
