research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617977-+   "citations": [
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617978-+    {
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617979-+     "fact": "L1",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617980-+     "source": "cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617981-+     "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:617982:+     "quote": "**Assume the Axiom of Choice** ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $\\kappa$ be an\ninfinite cardinal ([[def-cardinal]]). Then:\n\n**(a)** $\\kappa < \\kappa^{\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa)}$\n([[def-cardinal-arithmetic]], [[def-cofinality]]);\n\n**(b)** $\\operatorname{cf}(2^{\\kappa}) > \\kappa$;\n\n**(c)** in particular $\\operatorname{cf}(2^{\\aleph_0}) > \\aleph_0$\n([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]).\n\n**Clause (c) is a genuine restriction on the continuum, and it is proved in\nZFC rather than quoted.** It rules out every value of $2^{\\aleph_0}$ whose\ncofinality is $\\aleph_0$, and it selects none.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617983-+     "uses": [
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617984-+      "1.2"
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617985-+     ]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617986-+    },
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617987-+    {
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617988-+     "fact": "L1",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617989-+     "source": "def-cofinality",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617990-+     "source_section": "Definition",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:617991:+     "quote": "Let $\\alpha$ be an ordinal ([[def-ordinal]]). The **cofinality** of $\\alpha$ is\n\n$$\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\;:=\\; \\text{the least ordinal } \\beta \\text{ for which some } f : \\beta \\to \\alpha \\text{ has cofinal range},$$\n\ncofinal range meaning that $f[\\beta]$ is a cofinal subset of $\\alpha$\n([[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]): every $\\zeta \\in \\alpha$ satisfies\n$\\zeta \\le f(\\xi)$ for some $\\xi \\in \\beta$. That such a least ordinal exists, and\nthat a witnessing map of that length may be taken strictly increasing, is\n[[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]], and both are theorems of ZF. So\n$\\operatorname{cf}$ is defined at every ordinal, without any choice principle.\n\n**Regular and singular.** An **infinite cardinal** $\\kappa$\n([[def-cardinal]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]) is\n\n- **regular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) = \\kappa$;\n- **singular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) \\ne \\kappa$.\n\nThe two cases are exhaustive by definition, and by\n[[thm-cofinality-basics]] singular means exactly\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) < \\kappa$, since $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\le \\alpha$\nalways holds.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617992-+     "uses": [
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617993-+      "1.2"
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617994-+     ]
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617995-+    },
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617996-+    {
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617997-+     "fact": "L2",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617998-+     "source": "thm-regularity-of-the-alephs",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-617999-+     "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:618000:+     "quote": "Let $\\operatorname{cf}$, regular and singular be as in [[def-cofinality]], and\nlet $\\aleph_\\alpha$ be as in [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]. Then:\n\n**(a) In ZF.** $\\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_0) = \\aleph_0$, so $\\aleph_0$ is\nregular.\n\n**(b) Assuming the Axiom of Choice** ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]).\n$\\aleph_{\\alpha+1}$ is regular for every ordinal $\\alpha$.\n\n**(c) In ZF.** $\\operatorname{cf}(\\aleph_\\omega) = \\aleph_0$, and\n$\\aleph_0 < \\aleph_\\omega$, so $\\aleph_\\omega$ is **singular**.\n\n**(d) Assuming the Axiom of Choice.** Every infinite cardinal below\n$\\aleph_\\omega$ is regular, so $\\aleph_\\omega$ is the least singular infinite\ncardinal.\n\n**Clause (b) is where the Axiom of Choice becomes indispensable, and the\nhypothesis is not decoration.** The proof spends it once, to select an injection\n$g(\\xi) \\to \\aleph_\\alpha$ for each $\\xi$ below the cofinality, and there is no\ncanonical such family to fall back on: the sets $g(\\xi)$ are ordinals, but the\ninjections are not determined by them. Clauses (a), (c) and the classification\nhalf of (d) are choice free.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-618001-+     "uses": [
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-618002-+      "1.3"
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log-618003-+     ]
